{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1301873-what-exactly-was-the-sorcerers-crusade","id":1301873,"title":"What exactly was the Sorcerers Crusade?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-02T05:49:06-07:00","id":1301873,"title":"What exactly was the Sorcerers Crusade?","content":"This is something I've wondered about for years. The name sounds like a reference to something like a momentous event, or maybe as a term for the Order of Reason's general antagonism towards the Traditions but I can't find any instance of it being used outside of the title of the setting. Have I missed something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T11:54:41-07:00","id":1301962,"title":"","content":"Looking through the books...yeah, no. There is no in-game &quot;Sorcerers crusade&quot;. It can be seen of course as, yes, the crusade of the Order of Reason vs. the still forming Traditions. It certainly makes sense that this would be the time of 'The Sorcerers crusade'. Perhaps the olde time is referred to as that, in the mordern days, but by-the-book we got nothin' in-world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T12:06:02-07:00","id":1301969,"title":"","content":"It was a cool-sounding subtitle. That's all there really is to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T17:19:12-07:00","id":1302061,"title":"","content":"Well, Tezghul the Insane did lead a marauding horde from the Baltic States to central Europe before being stopped by the Order of Reason...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:57:03-07:00","id":1302100,"title":"","content":"It kinda-sorta refers to the start of the outright battle between the Order of Reason and the 9 Traditions after the Traditions actually formed, but for the most part someone just decided it was a cool title. <br /> <br /> (I ended up appropriating the name to refer to the Order of Hermes's militant reaction to discovering the Tremere betrayal.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T21:48:03-07:00","id":1302114,"title":"","content":"I would say it's probably just another name for the larger, history-spanning Ascension War. It's the set of conflicts between mages occurring during this time period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T01:35:58-07:00","id":1302143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1301873-what-exactly-was-the-sorcerers-crusade?p=1302100#post1302100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kinda-sorta refers to the start of the outright battle between the Order of Reason and the 9 Traditions after the Traditions actually formed, but for the most part someone just decided it was a cool title.<br /> <br /> (I ended up appropriating the name to refer to the Order of Hermes's militant reaction to discovering the Tremere betrayal.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of the Massassa War... I just don't get the 2nd Massassa War.<br /> <br /> &quot;We've just lost all of our Archmages and most of our legendary Wonders/Fetishes, along with all of our Horizon Holdings and a bunch of our ranks besides our greatest masters and most of our leaders. Now let's go to war with one of the most powerful Vampire Clans in the hope that we can steal back some books/objects they might have taken from us in the 1300s.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like it's just dumb enough that I am willing to accept that the Hermetics did it in a panic; sometimes people make bad decisions in fiction, it isn't a plot hole or anything. BUT it still beggars belief that they thought it would be a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T03:15:23-07:00","id":1302149,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1301873-what-exactly-was-the-sorcerers-crusade?p=1302114#post1302114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say it's probably just another name for the larger, history-spanning Ascension War.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did wonder if that was the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T10:48:42-07:00","id":1302268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1301873-what-exactly-was-the-sorcerers-crusade?p=1302143#post1302143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like it's just dumb enough that I am willing to accept that the Hermetics did it in a panic; sometimes people make bad decisions in fiction, it isn't a plot hole or anything. BUT it still beggars belief that they thought it would be a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>You kind of answered your own question there. The Order of Hermes wanted a win badly. Some of their number suggested attacking their prodigal House, and it just snowballed from there. Humans - even Awakened ones - can be make staggeringly stupid mistakes. And do so, all the time.<br /> <br /> It didn't help that the Order of Hermes knew basically nothing about House and Clan Tremere. Remember, in-universe people don't have access to the VtM books, with codified details about the powers, weaknesses, and scope of other Night Folk splats. What the Hermetics knew about Clan Tremere was what books could be scrounged up documenting the first Massasa War, and whatever House Tytalus's Tzimisce allies deigned to tell them.<br /> <br /> The Order of Hermes knew very little about who they were fighting. Thanks to the Dunning-Kruger Effect, they thought they already knew anything important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T11:13:12-07:00","id":1302276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1301873-what-exactly-was-the-sorcerers-crusade?p=1302268#post1302268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You kind of answered your own question there. The Order of Hermes wanted a win badly. Some of their number suggested attacking their prodigal House, and it just snowballed from there. Humans - even Awakened ones - can be make staggeringly stupid mistakes. And do so, all the time.<br /> <br /> It didn't help that the Order of Hermes knew basically nothing about House and Clan Tremere. Remember, in-universe people don't have access to the VtM books, with codified details about the powers, weaknesses, and scope of other Night Folk splats. What the Hermetics knew about Clan Tremere was what books could be scrounged up documenting the first Massasa War, and whatever House Tytalus's Tzimisce allies deigned to tell them.<br /> <br /> The Order of Hermes knew very little about who they were fighting. Thanks to the Dunning-Kruger Effect, they thought they already knew anything important.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good point. Probably didn't help that most of the wisest Hermetics were missing or dead, and people who are rushed/panicked do make poor decisions.<br /> <br /> Hadn't thought about the Hermetics having limited information on Vampires, that's important too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T11:30:12-07:00","id":1302281,"title":"","content":"Still the likes of Gilmore and Ibn-Thot, considering their rank, should know the whole history of the Order of Hermes, including the 1rst massa war and how it ended (and it's stated that at least Gilmore had some lore about vampires).<br /> <br /> That young mages fell for it isn't surprising (raiding fanged static mages for their grimoires? sure, sounds easy enough), but the leaders should have known better. Even after the first fireballs were casted they could (and should) have tried to defuse the conflict from the top, instead of fueling the fire like they did.<br /> <br /> In particular Gilmore it's to blame, it was amazingly naive for the Tytalus that's the leader of his House to fall <i>so completely</i> for the plot of that young charismatic upstart to get vampiric blood, and not realize anything was wrong until Tremere(Saulot?) felt the need to come and tell everyone.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I know the Order has laws against spying, but c'mon, that never stopped masters from doing it. A wizard from the circle of Klaus (Master entangled with vampires) so eager to go against the Tremere after his demise, and rising so quickly in popularity within the House at the same time. He had all the cards of being part of a conspiracy (or at least someone you would want to keep tabs on).<br /> <br /> But characterizing Hermetic leadership as detached and unwise it's as Traditional as the Traditions themselves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-03-2019, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T13:31:47-07:00","id":1303395,"title":"","content":"I just put it down as the order of reason's decision to crush the mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}